 ## Overview
-3D Texture Mapping renders a volumetric dataset by storing it as a 3D texture in GPU memory and resampling it using hardware-accelerated trilinear interpolation on planar polygons [S1, unofficial][S6, unofficial]. It solves the performance bottleneck of software ray casting by offloading the expensive interpolation and sampling steps to the graphics hardware's texture engine [S6, unofficial]. Unlike [Shear-Warp](shear-warp.md), which requires a final warp step and performs classification before resampling, this method performs trilinear interpolation followed by classification and compositing, resulting in higher image quality and consistent performance for perspective projections [S1, unofficial].
+3D Texture Mapping renders a volumetric dataset by storing it as a 3D texture in GPU memory and resampling it using hardware-accelerated trilinear interpolation on planar polygons [S1, unofficial][S6, unofficial]. It solves the performance bottleneck of software ray casting by offloading the expensive interpolation and sampling steps to the graphics hardware's texture engine [S6, unofficial]. Unlike [Shear-Warp](shear-warp.md), which requires a final warp step and performs classification before resampling, this method performs trilinear interpolation followed by classification and compositing, resulting in higher image quality and consistent performance for perspective projections [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [3D Texture Mapping](9529-3d-texture-mapping.md) by utilizing the hardware's ability to sample 3D texture coordinates on arbitrary polygons [S6, unofficial].
 
